<p>Notes:</p>
<p>The company reported an extraordinary loss in the second quarter of 1996 of $9 million on the retirement of debt. In the first half of 1997, the company reported an extraordinary loss of $17 million on the retirement of debt and an extraordinary loss of $35 million in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>Analysts consensus for the quarter is a loss of $0.14 per share, according to First Call.</p>
<p>On October 10, 1996, Time Warner acquired the remaining 80 percent interest in Turner Broadcasting System Inc (&quot;TBS&quot;) that it did not already own. The acquisition cost of about $6.2 billion was preliminarily allocated to the net assets acquired in accordance with the purchase method of accounting for business combinations.</p>
